 producer Ángel Pichardo Reyes. Its eight songs, all her own, take on dembow, reggaeton and Afrobeat; the street’s pulse, she said, is dembow."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Legacy","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Xiomara Fortuna belongs to the generation that brought Afro-Dominican roots into contemporary Dominican music, alongside figures such as "},{"type":"artistReference","attrs":{"occurrenceId":"2028fea7-ef92-4b31-a2ff-9f5856dd6946","artistId":"99537a98-fb19-4487-814d-c60d91c4d10b","displayText":"Luis \"Terror\" Días"}},{"type":"text","text":". The «alternative» label, she has said, names songwriters who built their work on that African heritage, and she regards the younger artists of that scene with a mother’s pride."}]}]}'::jsonb, 'published', id, 1 FROM artists WHERE slug = 'xiomara-fortuna'
